                    "Marketing a land parcel is a process of matching evidence to a likely user. A broad listing can create activity without producing a qualified result. A focused package can make a smaller pool of buyers more informed. Prepare a concise description of the acreage, boundary, access, terrain, utilities, current improvements, permitted or possible uses, and known constraints. Do not hide a defect, but do not overwhelm a buyer with every raw report either. The goal is informed decision-making. Distinguish facts supported by documents from the seller's interpretation of value and from forward-looking assumptions about a future approval.",
