                    "Concentration is a judgment about how several risks may interact. Holding adjacent parcels can create shared road, flood, water, market, or management exposure. Holding parcels for the same future use can concentrate demand exposure. Holding several assets with long approval dependencies can concentrate timing risk. Diversification by acreage or by purchase price does not automatically remove these links. Draw a simple correlation map and label common jurisdictions, utilities, access routes, uses, and buyers. Then decide whether the portfolio needs more cash reserves, a different holding period, or a staged sale plan.",
