                    "A concise memo is not a thin memo. It gives each important issue the space needed to be understood and assigns an owner to the next action. The property description should include enough location and physical context to avoid confusion, but it should not imply that a general description proves legal or financial suitability. The underwriting section should show the basis, improvement costs, carrying costs, reserve logic, exit scenario, and sensitivity variables. The risks section should say what would change the decision, not merely list generic categories such as market risk or permitting risk.",
